      {
        "id": 264832,
        "name": "",
        "username": "LonelyMan",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2026-01-14T16:39:37.877Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Listening to the Secretary Seized episode makes me feel like Crappy Legacy is the Aminia Twain of that universe, like his freedom five didn’t hire anyone to do that job so ACL himself is mired in the minutia of human legal and social responsibilities.  So he hardly ever does actual superhero things, but had the long-suffering “team parent” energy that Aminia usually has.</p>\n<p>It does mean that his dad and granddad would have been very well liked during the World Wars, because he literally was just another GI, not really powerful and certainly not living a charmed life.  Paul 8 has probably the worst of it, because America is less interested in hero worship of extremely normal people in the Sixties and forward; superhero stories are less about lionizing the courage of a vulnerable man who risks his life to protect others, and more about saying he has to spend all his time doing paperwork and paying bills like everyone else.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
